  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, showing that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation provides a large boost over singleprofile (+0.092 vs config_016). However, we have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool) for multiprofile, leaving open whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) could further improve performance. Question: config_020 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model setting, profile setting, RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion constant relative to config_018. This isolates the effect of aggregation method in the highest-performing regime. Why best: It is a clean single-variable extension of our current best, directly answers whether avgpool is sufficient or whether attention-based profile combination adds value, and the result will inform the aggregation choice for all subsequent multiprofile experiments (across RNA encoders and image encoders), making it the most information-dense next step under a limited budget."
